# Post-synthesis formal equivalence: dense_row_mac RTL vs its generic netlist.
# See synth/equiv_conv5x5_pe.ys for why this flow is shaped the way it is.
#
# This is the module whose reduction tree was originally a procedural `while`
# loop with a variable-stride `for` bound. It simulated correctly in both
# ModelSim and Icarus and was rejected outright by Yosys, and was rebuilt as an
# elaboration-time generate/genvar pairwise tree (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md). That
# history is the argument for checking it here: a construct that elaborates
# differently than it simulates is exactly what an RTL-vs-netlist proof catches,
# and the rebuilt tree had only ever been re-checked behaviourally.
#
# `memory` reports "Replacing memory \level with list of registers" on the gate
# side -- that is the reduction tree's intermediate array being mapped to
# flip-flops, which is expected, not a warning to silence.

read_verilog -sv rtl/dense_row_mac.sv
hierarchy -check -top dense_row_mac
proc
flatten
async2sync
opt_clean
design -stash gold

read_verilog -sv rtl/dense_row_mac.sv
hierarchy -check -top dense_row_mac
proc
opt
fsm
opt
memory
opt
techmap
opt
flatten
async2sync
opt_clean
design -stash gate

design -copy-from gold -as gold dense_row_mac
design -copy-from gate -as gate dense_row_mac
equiv_make gold gate equiv
hierarchy -top equiv
equiv_simple -short
equiv_simple
equiv_induct
equiv_status -assert
